Subject: [PATCH 0/2] usb: xhci: dbc: two fixes in the DbC core

Two fixes in xhci-dbgcap.c, found while running Linux's own DbC driver
against an emulation of the debug capability in QEMU:

1/2 DbC transfer rings fill after one lap (about 254 TRBs) since the
    num_trbs_free counter was removed, because nothing in the DbC driver
    advances ring->dequeue. ttyDBC goes quiet after roughly 254 KiB.
    Seen on 6.18.64; mainline has the same code.

2/2 Disabling the DbC gives back its requests before stopping it. A
    request queued in between is never given back and leaks its DMA
    mapping, and the controller can still write into buffers already
    given back. Found by reading the code and not seen in testing;
    covered by enable/disable cycles under traffic.

Josh Hoffer (2):
  usb: xhci: dbc: advance the transfer ring's dequeue pointer
  usb: xhci: dbc: stop the DbC before taking its requests back

 drivers/usb/host/xhci-dbgcap.c | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

